# No spelling rules for this language yet.

# Paradigm checks for find-accent-misspellings.py: a plain form is a real
# verb form when its stem plus an infinitive ending is a known word
# (acelero/aceleró: acelerar; limite/límite: limitar; critico/crítico: criticar).
paradigm-plain o ar er ir
paradigm-plain a ar er ir
paradigm-plain e ar er ir
paradigm-plain as ar er ir
paradigm-plain es ar er ir
paradigm-plain an ar er ir
paradigm-plain en ar er ir

# Imperatives and gerunds with pronouns take an accent (muéstrame, háblame):
# the list has some without (muestrame, hablame), so they were never fixed.
# The accent falls three or more syllables from the end.
respell-accent (?:me|te|se|nos|os)?(?:lo|la|le|los|las|les)?|(?:me|te|se|nos|os) [áéíóú](?:[^aeiouáéíóú]*[aeiou]+){2,}[^aeiou]*$
# Conversational words (déjame, cuéntame) are in Tatoeba, rarely in Common
# Voice: a word seen this often in Tatoeba is added.
one-source 20 tatoeba
